Build in the extension directory and load it with PHP of the same version, architecture, thread safety and debug configuration. For Windows targets see [Building for Windows]($link.page('development/windows')).

# [Linux and macOS]($heading.id('unix'))

```sh
zig build -Dphp-include-dir="$(php-config --include-dir)"
php -n -dextension=./modules/my_php_extension.so -r 'hello();'
```

The skeleton produces `modules/my_php_extension.so`. `-n` skips `php.ini` and `-dextension` loads the module for that process. This example calls the skeleton's `hello()` function.

Debug is the default. For an optimized build with Zig runtime safety checks, use:

```sh
zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSafe -Dphp-include-dir="$(php-config --include-dir)"
```

See [Build options]($link.page('advanced/build-options')) for LTO and ZTS resource caching.

From the extension project directory, use the SDK build script to cross-compile shared extensions on Linux. Select the exact published PHP version and target. NTS is the default. Pass additional Zig options after `--`.

```sh
/path/to/phpz/scripts/build-unix.sh --php-version 8.2.36 --target aarch64-linux-gnu --zts -- -Doptimize=ReleaseFast
/path/to/phpz/scripts/build-unix.sh --php-version 8.2.36 --target x86_64-linux-musl
/path/to/phpz/scripts/build-unix.sh --php-version 8.2.36 --target aarch64-macos
```

Verified SDKs are cached under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/phpz/sdk` (default `~/.cache/phpz/sdk`). Builds for the same PHP version, target, and thread-safety mode reuse the cached headers.

From Windows PowerShell, use the same SDKs and targets. The default cache is `%LOCALAPPDATA%/phpz/sdk`. Add `-Zts` for a thread-safe PHP build.

```powershell
C:\path\to\phpz\scripts\build-unix.ps1 -PhpVersion 8.2.36 -Target aarch64-linux-gnu -ZigArgs @('-Doptimize=ReleaseFast')
```

Run `Get-Help C:\path\to\phpz\scripts\build-unix.ps1 -Full` to see all parameters and examples.

# [Loading the extension with php.ini]($heading.id('configure-loading'))

After testing a single load, add `extension=/absolute/path/to/my_php_extension.so` to the target PHP configuration. Use the actual DLL path on Windows. Use `php --ini` to locate the CLI configuration and `php --ri my_php_extension` to verify the module. PHP-FPM and Apache may read different configuration files. Reload or restart the service.

# [Troubleshooting]($heading.id('troubleshooting'))

| Symptom | What to check |
| --- | --- |
| Missing PHP headers | Check `php-config --include-dir`. Use the full path to the target's `php-config` if multiple versions are installed. |
| Load failure or ABI mismatch | Compare `php -v`, `php-config --version`, architecture, NTS/ZTS and debug settings. On Windows also match the import library. |
| One-off load works but configured load fails | Use `php --ini` for the CLI. Check the service SAPI's configuration and reload its processes. |
| Old signature or binding after editing a stub | Run `zig build gen-stub`, rebuild and load the new module. |
| `Zig requires ... parameters` or a reference declaration error | Fix differences in argument counts, optional or variadic parameters and reference flags. Use a context-only handler for manual parsing when appropriate. |
| `@frameless-function` binding fails | phpz does not export frameless handlers. Remove the annotation and regenerate arginfo. |
| `gen-stub` fails | Check tokenizer, write access to `build/` and network and download tools for the initial PHP-Parser installation. |
| `evaluation exceeded ... backwards branches` | phpz sets internal compile-time branch quotas based on declarations or parameter counts. Check whether the diagnostic points into phpz or your own `comptime` code. |
| `expectArgs declaration mismatch` | Zig Debug detected inconsistent required/fixed counts or a variadic flag between arginfo and the parser specification. Synchronize the stub, generated header and handler. |

Function and method binding, argument parsing, INI collection and module registration adjust their own quotas. Ordinary extensions do not need a global `@setEvalBranchQuota`. Manage quotas for your own compile-time work separately.

Run [PHPT tests]($link.page('development/testing')) after building. For `phpize` or PHP source builds see [Integration with the PHP build system]($link.page('development/php-build-system')).
